---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="About" description="Who's behind egusto.">
  <section class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-16">
    <h1 class="mb-8 font-serif text-4xl font-semibold sm:text-5xl">About</h1>
    <div class="prose-post !mx-0">
      <p>
        I'm <strong>Alois Seneka</strong>, and egusto is where I write up my applied AI work: the
        parts that don't make it into a client deck. Mostly that's notes on using AI tools day to
        day, what turns into a reusable Claude Skill, what doesn't, and what breaks along the way.
      </p>
      <p>
        I keep an eye on the apps and services drawing big audiences at any given time, then
        tinker with Claude to see how far those ideas can be rebuilt. If it works, it ends up here.
        If it doesn't, that usually ends up here too.
      </p>
      <p>
        The <a href="/store/">Skill-Store</a> has some of the Claude Skills I've built for my own
        work. A few are free to download, and a few are paid, for people who want the finished
        version instead of building it themselves.
      </p>

      <h2>How the posts are made</h2>
      <p>
        I draft and refine posts with Claude, make the cover images in Canva, and publish them
        to this site as plain Markdown files. There's no CMS.
      </p>

      <h2>Get in touch</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Email: <a href="mailto:asseneka@gmail.com">asseneka@gmail.com</a></li>
        <li>Facebook Messenger: <a href="https://www.facebook.com/asseneka47015" target="_blank" rel="noopener">facebook.com/asseneka47015</a></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
